  "goodToKnow": "Die Doktorarbeit is a doctoral thesis, officially die Dissertation; to do one is promovieren. The Dr. title is highly valued in Germany and appears on doorbells and ID cards. In 2011, defence minister Karl-Theodor zu Guttenberg resigned after large parts of his Doktorarbeit were found to be plagiarised, exposed by the online project GuttenPlag; other politicians followed. Plural: die Doktorarbeiten."
